hat's quite important is deal with  fortunes injuries and he uses the word  in urea there and it helps to lead us to  tranquility the the Epicureans and Greek  expressed this as octave axia not being  troubled sister Oh uses the word  tranquilly talks in Latin which is what  we can translate as peacefulness or  contentment or tranquility so wisdom as  a virtue as something cultivated within  oneself  is going to be valuable from the  epicurean perspective for all of these  reasons that we've talked about because  it's going to make us so we use a  synonym of wisdom it's going to make us  more prudent in deciding which pleasures  to select and to pursue and enjoy and  which to set aside which desires to say  no to and also which pains need to be  endured at least for the moment in order  to lead to greater pleasures later on  and which pains we can avoid in which we  can even see to be generated by  ourselves in the ways that we think  about things so by that  sort of  reasoning wisdom would become the most  important of the virtues for an  epicurean but it's not valuable in its  own right  you
 

